# Files that end up inside a Linux container must keep LF endings.
#
# Git on Windows converts to CRLF on checkout, and a shell script carrying `\r`
# fails in the image with errors that name the carriage return rather than the
# problem ("set: not found", "\r: command not found"). It builds fine on the
# machine that wrote the file and breaks for whoever clones it next, which is
# the worst shape a bug can take.
#
# Deliberately narrow — normalising the whole repository would rewrite every
# file in the working tree on the next checkout.
*.sh       text eol=lf
*.envsh    text eol=lf
*.template text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
